# DotVibes shell — .env_usr template.
#
# The REAL file lives at ~/.config/bash/.env_usr — LOCAL-ONLY, never
# committed anywhere (it holds credentials/tokens/machine-specific values).
# This commented example documents its expected shape. The shell component's
# install.sh copies it into place (comments-only, perms 600) when no real
# .env_usr exists yet, and never overwrites an existing one.
#
# Shared, non-sensitive variables (paths reused by several scripts, skills,
# ...) belong in the tracked bash/env_vars instead.
#
# Sourced by ~/.bashrc right AFTER .env_vars (so anything here can override a
# shared default) and before PATH/aliases/prompt — also in non-interactive
# shells.
#
# Keep values quoted if they contain special characters; example:

#export YOUTRACK_URL="https://your-instance.myjetbrains.com"
#export YOUTRACK_TOKEN="perm:..."
#export YOUTRACK_ONLY_MINE=1
#export EXAMPLE_USER="someone"

# Anything the tools export implicitly (e.g. GCC_COLORS) also belongs here so
# it survives a .bashrc reset:
#export GCC_COLORS='error=01;31:warning=01;35:note=01;36:caret=01;32:locus=01:quote=01'
